---
// Section 4: Modern Bento FAQ Accordion with GSAP items reveal
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What does YP Nexus Foundation stand for?",
    a: "YP Nexus Foundation (Paryay Parisanstha) is a registered charitable trust in Pune, India. It provides alternatives towards an ecologically sensitive life in the interconnected spheres of open learning, community habitats, grassroots research (PiSELT), and documentary media (TurTle Media).",
    category: "Foundation"
  },
  {
    q: "Is Paryay Dschool an approved or affiliated NIOS school?",
    a: "Paryay Dschool is not an affiliated or franchise school; it is an alternative learning sanctuary that works towards open schooling. Learners study through experiential frameworks and appear independently for official 10th and 12th board examinations through NIOS (National Institute of Open Schooling) or MsBOS (Maharashtra State Board of Open Schooling), both fully accredited for all higher education degrees.",
    category: "Open Schooling"
  },
  {
    q: "Why are there no conventional textbooks, rote exams, or homework?",
    a: "Traditional schooling relies on competitive grading and rote memorization that often disconnects children from real life. At Paryay, learning is built on Fundamental Learning Methodology (FLM)—connecting learners directly with soil, tools, nature, life trades, and practical problem-solving. Each learner's progress is documented individually rather than judged by marks.",
    category: "Methodology"
  },
  {
    q: "How does the dedicated 1:6 mentor-to-learner ratio work?",
    a: "Unlike crowded classrooms with 40 to 60 students per teacher, one experienced mentor closely guides only 6 learners. This allows mentors to identify each child's unique capabilities, facilitate their emotional and intellectual growth, and conduct regular joint reviews with parents.",
    category: "Mentoring"
  },
  {
    q: "What are Expedition Visits (EVs) and Biodiversity Journeys (JEEVs)?",
    a: "Regular off-campus study expeditions where learners travel into rural ecosystems, forests, craft centers, and agricultural habitats. Children learn geography, ecology, sociology, and practical trades through direct sensory immersion and field notes.",
    category: "Field Study"
  },
  {
    q: "What is the Vartul FLM guidance course for Parents and Grandparents?",
    a: "Parenting is an essential co-learning journey. Through our Vartul FLM Service Center, we conduct ongoing 18-session courses ('Understanding Learning for Parents & Grands') helping families understand child brain development, reduce screen dependence, and create a supportive learning ecology at home.",
    category: "Parenting"
  },
  {
    q: "What programs are available under YP Nexus?",
    a: "We offer an entire learning continuum: Balmitee (ages 3–8), PND Novice Dschool (ages 8–12), Paryay Juvenile Dschool (ages 12–20), yPOLEN for open university students, WAI (75-day capability diagnostic), and NeRo screen-free intergenerational learning (ages 2 to 100).",
    category: "Programs"
  }
];
---

<section id="faq" class="w-full py-16 sm:py-24 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-canvas">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto space-y-10 sm:space-y-14">
    
    <!-- Section Header -->
    <div class="reveal-item text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto space-y-3">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-lime-subtle border border-lime-accent/50 text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-dark font-bold">
        <span>04 / Inquiries &amp; Answers</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold text-ink-900 tracking-tight">
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-ink-600 leading-relaxed">
        Key details about our alternative learning methodology, official accreditation, and admissions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Modern Bento Accordions -->
    <div class="space-y-3 sm:space-y-4">
      {faqs.map((faq, idx) => (
        <details class={`reveal-item reveal-delay-${(idx % 4) + 1} group bg-white rounded-2xl sm:rounded-3xl p-5 sm:p-7 border border-ink-200/80 shadow-xs hover:border-lime-accent transition-all duration-200 open:shadow-card open:border-lime-accent`}>
          <summary class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer list-none gap-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 sm:gap-4">
              <span class="w-7 h-7 sm:w-8 sm:h-8 rounded-full bg-lime-subtle text-brand-dark flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-xs shrink-0">
                0{idx + 1}
              </span>
              <span class="font-display text-base sm:text-xl font-bold text-ink-900 group-hover:text-brand-forest transition-colors">
                {faq.q}
              </span>
            </div>

            <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-canvas border border-ink-200 flex items-center justify-center text-ink-700 shrink-0 group-open:rotate-180 group-open:bg-lime-accent group-open:text-ink-900 transition-all duration-300">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-ink-100 text-xs sm:text-sm text-ink-700 leading-relaxed font-normal pl-10 sm:pl-12">
            <p>{faq.a}</p>
            <span class="inline-block mt-3 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-md text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider bg-canvas text-ink-500 font-bold">
              {faq.category}
            </span>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
